You recall a book you recently read about Robinson Crusoe. Once on the island, Robinson spent his first night in a tree to avoid predator attacks. Good idea! It's useful to read books after all!

It's fortunate that you and your friends won the cup of Mech-City in tree climbing. In no time, you find a suitable tree and climb it. Resting on the branches might not be as comfortable as on the ground, but it's certainly safer.

Meanwhile, darkness falls, and the sounds of the night jungle surround you. It would be wise to take a nap to conserve strength for tomorrow.